        // We'll deploy a simple rejector in setUp? Not allowed to define other contracts. So use address(0) which is special: call to address(0) always returns true. That won't diverge.
        // Instead, we can make the call fail by having insufficient balance? 
        // The contract has 1 ether, we send 1 ether, should succeed. But to cause failure, we need to send more than balance? 
        // If we send 1 ether exactly, it succeeds. If we send 2 ether, it would revert in both because require(balance >= amount) in .call? Actually .call{value:...} with value > address(this).balance reverts in callee? No, it reverts at call site because insufficient balance. So both revert? Actually in reference, the require would catch the false and revert; in bug, __sent_result100 is false but ignored, so no revert. But the call to .call itself will revert if insufficient balance? Let's check: calling .call with value > balance of contract causes the call to revert immediately, so __sent_result100 is never assigned, the whole transaction reverts. So both revert. So that doesn't work.
